# Tech Stack
This project uses:
- Node.js + Express backend
- MongoDB + Mongoose (or Prisma if SQL)
- React (or Next.js if applicable)
- JWT authentication
- REST API conventions

# Folder Structure
Backend:
- /src
  - /models
  - /controllers
  - /routes
  - /middlewares
  - /services
  - /utils
  - /config

Frontend:
- /src
  - /components
  - /pages or /routes
  - /hooks
  - /context
  - /services
  - /utils

# Conventions
- camelCase for variables/functions
- PascalCase for components/models
- All API responses follow { success, data, message }
- Use async/await everywhere
- Error handling through middleware
- Keep controllers thin; move logic to services
- Reusable form components

# Database
- MongoDB
- Connections through /config/db.js
- All models in /models with schemas in separate files

# Auth
- JWT stored in httpOnly cookies
- Auth middleware required for protected routes

# API Versioning
Base URL: /api/v1
